                <pb facs="0535" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg529"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Cusack-Smith to the Marquis of
                        Salisbury.—Received April 4.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Navigators Islands, April 4; inclosure in note from Sir J.
                    Pauncefote of April 28, 1892, section 1.]</p>
                <p rendition="#center">No. 1.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copy of a
                    letter received last night from Mr. Stevenson, forwarding to me the texts of
                    parts of the Berlin treaty as altered toy a committee and approved by a public
                    meeting.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. B.
                    Cusack-Smith.</hi></signed></closer>




